Barfaee's laughing stopped as he recognized that you've slain Astaroth, the
demon summoned by Barfaee. Barfaees eyes, while still not having lost their
distrust, show hardly controlled fear. Now novices, priests, and zealots ar-
rive, attracted by the noise of the battle. Only they are the reason that Bar-
faee stays calm. Still staring at you, he speaks to the crowd. "My children",
he starts, surprisingly soft, "the One has sent me a vision." He stops, ob-
viously thinking. "A vision of great trust in our goal." He stops again. His
eyes glance around, as he recognizes the people not listening, but chatting
with each other, nervously. "I AM HER CHOSEN ONE", Barfaee shouts. "SHE SENT
A MINION TO GIVE ME HER GIFT!! With this sword" --he points to Northdoom-- "I
will be able to take revenge on everybody who denies our superiority! I AM--"
As soon as he touches it, Northdoom dissolves to dust. "No!!" Barfaee screams,
turns around, stares at the crowd, unsure what to do. And suddenly everything
is quiet. "He has betrayed you." A new voice fills the halls, a voice both far
away, and inside the head's of everybody. "Thus, he has fallen. His greed was
too much for him." Panically the crowd shouts and screams. "This is the end of
your conspiracy", the voice says. "I am Hermes, one of the divines you chose
to deny. I speak to you---directly, without needing an apostle. And I speak:
Make an end to this! Return to your families! Leave that sorry old man alone."
And Barfaee is sitting in his throne, embittered, but with no power at all.